><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T13:01:25-07:00","id":1374201,"title":"","content":"So I am currently just skimming through the book, but I must say that I really like the new Tremere mechanics and most of the fluff. I'm not really sure how I feel about the fact that vampires are no longer strongly connected to the Tremere, as that connection was the defining trait and point of origin for them. I am also disappointed that the Banishers chapter did not update the Timori (I think they are not even mentioned in the book). It is full of a lot of other goodness in Legacies and Nameless Orders, and the Ziggurats are awesome, and the new interpretation of the Sixth Watchtower seems to align to the famously lost Blood of Atlantis, so it is not bad- but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T13:17:58-07:00","id":1374210,"title":"","content":"The whole &quot;6th, much more powerful path with a terrible cost&quot; thing is fun. Obviously going to want to be a Tremere, bad. But like, being a Tremere is *too* appealing to me. They're just remarkably powerful this incarnation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T13:38:08-07:00","id":1374216,"title":"","content":"Dear Authors: Thank you for including Pangloss.<br /> <br /> I look forward to all the times my players will punch him in the dick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T13:44:30-07:00","id":1374221,"title":"","content":"I am ...i cannot find the right word.<br /> The cover is...strange. Very, unusual.<br /> It is a joke?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T14:47:55-07:00","id":1374231,"title":"","content":"....am i weird for wanting to play a Nasnasi? Like they don't seem that bad((they aren't Nephandi after all)) and I think playing one who accidentally ended up in Dur-Abzu rather than deliberately decided to go down that route could be a compelling character.<br /> <br /> Tremere as always are win &lt;3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T15:33:28-07:00","id":1374243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1374231#post1374231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....am i weird for wanting to play a Nasnasi? Like they don't seem that bad((they aren't Nephandi after all)) and I think playing one who accidentally ended up in Dur-Abzu rather than deliberately decided to go down that route could be a compelling character.<br /> <br /> Tremere as always are win &lt;3</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, you ain't the only one. There's a level of inherent tragedy to one given how the pinnacle of Joining is a personal hell, but there's something darkly majestic about them. I can even see one befriending a normal cabal without aiming to corrupt them (too much).<br /> <br /> Mostly because it'd be Abridged Vincent Valentine x1000<br /> <br /> &quot;I haven't had new company since a family of spiders laid eggs in my bones...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T18:28:51-07:00","id":1374266,"title":"","content":"I can\u2019t believe I missed this one. Now I have it, and I\u2019m pretty happy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1374201#post1374201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am also disappointed that the Banishers chapter did not update the Timori (I think they are not even mentioned in the book).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Timori has two things against them:<br /> <br /> 1) They were an artifact of the first edition\u2019s rather different take on the orders and Atlantis that don\u2019t make any sense in 2e\u2019s paradigm (wherein the orders are not literally continuations of social structures from the Time Before but rather syncretic creations of the historical period that are as much responsible for the prevailing myth of the Time Before as anything, which itself gives their symbols power). And it\u2019s not like a bunch of Banishers is going to bother cooking up a story about how they\u2019re the inheritors of some Atlantean order.<br /> <br /> 2) Not that anyone but me cares about these things, but \u201cTimori\u201d is firmly in the uncanny valley of godawful fake Latin, where you can tell what word root they\u2019re trying to invoke, but that\u2019s definitely not how to do it, and in fact it means something entirely different from what they clearly intend it to mean. So yeah, let that word die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 03-11-2020, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T19:38:04-07:00","id":1374277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1374201#post1374201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I am currently just skimming through the book, but I must say that I really like the new Tremere mechanics and most of the fluff. I'm not really sure how I feel about the fact that vampires are no longer strongly connected to the Tremere, as that connection was the defining trait and point of origin for them. I am also disappointed that the Banishers chapter did not update the Timori (I think they are not even mentioned in the book). It is full of a lot of other goodness in Legacies and Nameless Orders, and the Ziggurats are awesome, and the new interpretation of the Sixth Watchtower seems to align to the famously lost Blood of Atlantis, so it is not bad- but still.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't mind, because the Tremere are officially Magic Nazis now. What makes you think they're going to remember a meaningless detail like being inspired by those dirty leeches taking Awakened jobs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T19:38:42-07:00","id":1374278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1374216#post1374216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dear Authors: Thank you for including Pangloss.<br /> <br /> I look forward to all the times my players will punch him in the dick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you notice the shade in the PDF bookmarks? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T21:21:07-07:00","id":1374291,"title":"","content":"Starting reading it, more for new rules than NPCs. I started with advised on conflict between mages in Introduction as got problem with them when running game last time - and <b>Nameless and Accursed</b> advises felt very lacking. They are generalizations of what we know from all 1E - I still have problems to make challenging fights with mages on mages in 2E conflicts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Not enough 'meat' or 'teeth' in this part of book.<br /> <br /> And optional rule 'I know you Imago, so I can counter your spells better' does not seem to fit with mages conflict that works on simple 'who shoots first'. Once you 'shoot' spell, you win. There is no second take on it needed. Or at least this is how 2E game felt to me when running it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T21:41:29-07:00","id":1374294,"title":"","content":"Is it just me or does almost every legacy attainment in this book break at least one of the attainment creation rules? So many of them use 2+ reach on attainments that should only have 1 reach available and some only have 1 reach used when they should have 2 reach available to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T23:51:45-07:00","id":1374302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1374277#post1374277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't mind, because the Tremere are officially Magic Nazis now. What makes you think they're going to remember a meaningless detail like being inspired by those dirty leeches taking Awakened jobs?</div> </div> </div> </div> I did not notice the nazi part :O. Are they magical racists or just normal racists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T02:41:00-07:00","id":1374311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1374266#post1374266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Timori has two things against them:<br /> <br /> 1) They were an artifact of the first edition\u2019s rather different take on the orders and Atlantis that don\u2019t make any sense in 2e\u2019s paradigm (wherein the orders are not literally continuations of social structures from the Time Before but rather syncretic creations of the historical period that are as much responsible for the prevailing myth of the Time Before as anything, which itself gives their symbols power). And it\u2019s not like a bunch of Banishers is going to bother cooking up a story about how they\u2019re the inheritors of some Atlantean order.<br /> <br /> 2) Not that anyone but me cares about these things, but \u201cTimori\u201d is firmly in the uncanny valley of godawful fake Latin, where you can tell what word root they\u2019re trying to invoke, but that\u2019s definitely not how to do it, and in fact it means something entirely different from what they clearly intend it to mean. So yeah, let that word die.</div> </div> </div> </div>If anything, those points are what that makes me want to see them revised and updated- I like the core themes and concepts behind the Legacy, yet it requires some good updates and modifications to fit 2e- so yeah, I won't say that those points are against them as much as they are the reasons for why they need a revision, and Nameless and Accursed could have been a good place to introduce such update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T04:28:14-07:00","id":1374319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1374302#post1374302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did not notice the nazi part :O. Are they magical racists or just normal racists?</div> </div> </div> </div>Magical racists. To them, anyone with a greater template and isn't a mage is a child of the Sixth Watchtower, and thus inherently corrupted, as are Supernal beings while they're in the Fallen World; all inherent restrictions and weaknesses are symptoms of it, and thus the Tremere have a duty to destroy them before they entrap other mages worse than even the original Watchtowers do, or enslave them in order to get some good out of their state.<br /> <br /> There's also a rather cynical motive in there; for greater templates, a Tremere can't steal their souls... <i>or </i>if they can, their souls are just as long-lasting as another mage's. Which means that the Tremere doesn't need to murder people who, in another world, might have been their peers (Beasts, Unchained, Prometheans, Arisen, and Bound are immune, but everyone else is on the menu). So, to the Tremere, they get what they see as a less morally suspect couple months by stealing the life of what they feel to be an inferior, and their ideology has been made to agree with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T07:06:02-07:00","id":1374340,"title":"","content":"the one thing i am now pondering after seeing Nasnasi, are if there are human beings who find some way to draw power from the Abyss without being an awakened mage first. Might be something to homebrew as a template later *hmmms*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T09:26:48-07:00","id":1374364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1374340#post1374340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the one thing i am now pondering after seeing Nasnasi, are if there are human beings who find some way to draw power from the Abyss without being an awakened mage first. Might be something to homebrew as a template later *hmmms*</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there IS that mage (from Unbidden I think) who Awakened directly to a Ziggurat (or, at the very least, was heavily hinted to be so). Need to double check it, of course.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Correction, it is in Intruders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 03-12-2020, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T13:38:36-07:00","id":1374409,"title":"","content":"Hmm.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised by the degree of mechanical similarity between some of the new Scelesti mechanics and the rough 2E Conversion I made a couple of years back. Maybe it was better than I gave it credit for at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T16:01:02-07:00","id":1374442,"title":"","content":"The Gnosis tendencies are too high imo, for what you get out of the various forms of corrupted mages. For example, defiled spells are supposed to be a gateway, but they use Gnosis for abyssal reaches, and require very high Gnosis to be worthwhile. Instead of rolling Gnosis, I would more suggest something like (10-Gnosis) autosuccesses, to make spell defiling darkly tempting to newer mages. The quick path to power and all that.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I kind of think &quot;roll Gnosis or become a preta&quot; for new Tremere is a bit overly punitive -- low Gnosis mages are already disadvantaged. I would suggest Gnosis+highest subtle arcanum. I would also lower the requirements on Tremere soul grappling. There is simply unlikely to be much incentive for grappling at the ridiculously high levels.<br /> <br /> Finally, Stress fills up a bit slowly. A Rapt needs to be thwarted about six times to fill their Stress track on average, and most of the time will only release Lesser Tulpa. Rapt are supposedly NPCs, but their iconic mechanic means that unless a Rapt is not only in every scene but avoids their Fault constantly, nothing is likely to happen. Also, does fulfilling your Fault empty Stress? <br /> <br /> Essentially, the tendency is for villain options to be weighted to far, far beyond becoming a Master, the point at which whatever mechanical distinctions of the accursed mage are overshadowed by the supreme power of mastery. The opposite tendency would be better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T18:08:50-07:00","id":1374465,"title":"","content":"Note to self; &quot;Grant wisdom to/Save (npc name) from their Harrowed Awkening&quot; is a valid Obsession. Still might not be possible and will get you in trouble with the Arcane Law.<br /> <br /> Also the next step in the 'Crown of Roses' project has a better chance of creating a Walker or a Harrowed than succeeding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T18:19:39-07:00","id":1374467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1374442#post1374442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gnosis stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I've noticed this too. It stuck out back when Scelesti mechanics were first mentioned in the 2E core, and it sticks out more now. At first, I wondered if it was just part of how the gameline as a whole incentivizes raising your power stat far, far (seriously, ludicrously <i><b>far</b></i>) more than others do, and honestly, that may well be what it is. It's totally reasonable in-universe, too, to have these sorts of antagonists all be experienced Mages, and it <i>does</i> accurately reflect how dangerous pursuing these paths is meant to be for a novice.<br /> <br /> But even if that is the case, and this is an intentional design decision...you're not wrong that it basically rules these options out for lower-Gnosis characters, and therefore, as player options at most tables. Of course, this is an antagonist book, I recognize that, but...well, it'd be nice if it weren't the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T19:23:00-07:00","id":1374475,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, almost all the other games tries to dissuade the player from reaching powerstat 6+, either by raising the drawbacks way too high or by simply not having any content geared towards such characters. For many of the games the scale could just as well stop at five dots, so I very much welcome this.<br /> It sucks that you can't have them as direct antagonists for low-Gnosis PCs, but my fix is to bump up the PCs for games featuring Tremere and Scelesti. Start with raised Gnosis, additional Arcana dots and a bunch of XP. They are grave threats in the setting, so it makes sense to play experienced mages and not those who just came out of wizard school. I mean, a lowly Gnosis 1 mage should be a snack for the average Tremere, or horribly unprepared to properly deal with the Abyss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-12-2020, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T20:07:21-07:00","id":1374480,"title":"","content":"To be fair the other games don't include the power stat in dice rolls as regularly as mage, so not having a higher one doesn't make as big of a difference. Disciplines and Gifts don't use the power stat. Contracts use Wyrd, but similar to mages, there are very few downsides to raising it. <br /> <br /> Iirc, Dave B wrote that most mages will be at Gnosis 3 within a year or two of Awakening, and that half of all mages have Gnosis 5 or above (though very few above 7).<br /> <br /> Given all of that it makes sense that mages should run high on Gnosis, even PCs, and the Tremere power curve seems more reasonable for a PC or an antagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 03-12-2020, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T23:01:30-07:00","id":1374507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1374475#post1374475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sucks that you can't have them as direct antagonists for low-Gnosis PCs, but my fix is to bump up the PCs for games featuring Tremere and Scelesti. Start with raised Gnosis, additional Arcana dots and a bunch of XP. They are grave threats in the setting, so it makes sense to play experienced mages and not those who just came out of wizard school. I mean, a lowly Gnosis 1 mage should be a snack for the average Tremere, or horribly unprepared to properly deal with the Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind mismatched Gnosis antagonists so much as that the tremendous Gnosis/Hallow requirements tends to put this stuff way back past the point of relevancy. Its hard to make grapples relevant at power stat 5 in Mage, let alone 9; its hard to make 1-2 free reaches relevant at any point, and greater tulpa look like they will almost never show up at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T11:35:38-07:00","id":1375126,"title":"","content":"I like the overview of the Rapt. It singularly helps sum up the nature of Wisdom as not morality but the ability to contain your powers and keep your obsessions in check. It goes back to Dave calling out Dresden as low Wisdom: it is not because he is immoral, but because he is constantly willing to make deals, throw spells and ask questions later, and not consider consequences in his obsession to protect his friends and the mortals in his city. Plus as a physician who works daily with individuals with mental health issues, it is nice to see the shift in terminology and movement away from the connotations of \u201cthe Mad.\u201d <br /> <br /> Cannot wait to delve further into this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T23:18:28-07:00","id":1375226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1374221#post1374221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am ...i cannot find the right word.<br /> The cover is...strange. Very, unusual.<br /> It is a joke?</div> </div> </div> </div>This looks to be a scene from one of the short fictions scattered throughout the books, I don't remember which right off.<br /> In this scene the Acanthus wearing the Union Jack dress was working as a DJ in a club when she used her magic against a man in the crowd. I don't remember it being rich on details but whatever she was doing had her questioning whether it was right, while justifying herself based on what he had done.<br /> It was a scene of a Mage pushing her ethical limits to stop someone who had broken those limits.<br /> Very appropriate for the topic of this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T04:54:20-07:00","id":1375259,"title":"","content":"So Left Hand Path 2: Electric Boogaloo is neat.<br /> <br /> (I kid, it's definitely more than that, but it's good)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T15:15:41-07:00","id":1375327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1375226#post1375226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This looks to be a scene from one of the short fictions scattered throughout the books, I don't remember which right off.<br /> In this scene the Acanthus wearing the Union Jack dress was working as a DJ in a club when she used her magic against a man in the crowd. I don't remember it being rich on details but whatever she was doing had her questioning whether it was right, while justifying herself based on what he had done.<br /> It was a scene of a Mage pushing her ethical limits to stop someone who had broken those limits.<br /> Very appropriate for the topic of this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, this make a lot more sense now!<br /> I was surprised about a cover with an explicit innuendo, never expected.<br /> I truly was taken a back <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T15:36:48-07:00","id":1375328,"title":"","content":"You know, I have just thought about how funny it is that the Tremere can't steal the Horrors of Beasts, but the Flayer from Orkney (I think) does, as he was heavily hinted to be a Reaper by himself. No wonder that the Tremere are hunting him- I mean, the Flayer supposedly succeeding where the Tremere fail is more than a mockery to their traditions. It is a threat for their supposed superiority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 03-17-2020, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T15:58:31-07:00","id":1375332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1375328#post1375328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I have just thought about how funny it is that the Tremere can't steal the Horrors of Beasts, but the Flayer from Orkney (I think) does, as he was heavily hinted to be a Reaper by himself. No wonder that the Tremere are hunting him- I mean, the Flayer supposedly succeeding where the Tremere fail is more than a mockery to their traditions. It is a threat for their supposed superiority.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can, but it's just that the Horror isn't a soul so their Tremere powers can't do it. They just have to resort to spells like regular mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T16:21:32-07:00","id":1375338,"title":"","content":"I haven't gotten to their section in N&amp;A but in first edition a driving force among the Tremere was finding new kinds of reapers and absorbing their legacies into them. Our story had someone who seemed to be acting like a new kind of reaper and the Tremere (and another House) were arriving to steal their secrets just as the players were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T01:02:05-07:00","id":1375557,"title":"","content":"So, are the Tremere supposed to be the Lower Depth counterparts to Scelesti now? Is the 'Seventh Dragon' that spoke to them at Chur implied to be some sort of demon they feed souls to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T13:00:15-07:00","id":1375675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1375557#post1375557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, are the Tremere supposed to be the Lower Depth counterparts to Scelesti now? Is the 'Seventh Dragon' that spoke to them at Chur implied to be some sort of demon they feed souls to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Explicitly an open question.<br /> <br /> The &quot;they're sacrificing souls to a thing from the Lower Depths&quot; explanation is called out as having holes in it within the text; the Captivity, their enslavement of gods and monsters, and the encounter with the Seventh Dragon all make up an extremely confounded history that individual game tables can make of what they will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T12:12:42-07:00","id":1375840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1375328#post1375328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I have just thought about how funny it is that the Tremere can't steal the Horrors of Beasts, but the Flayer from Orkney (I think) does, as he was heavily hinted to be a Reaper by himself. No wonder that the Tremere are hunting him- I mean, the Flayer supposedly succeeding where the Tremere fail is more than a mockery to their traditions. It is a threat for their supposed superiority.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is the Flayer described?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T12:29:37-07:00","id":1375842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1375840#post1375840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where is the Flayer described?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Orkney setting in the Beast: the Primordial corebook. The discussion where we put this together can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1046759-the-flayer-insatiable?p=1047085#post1047085\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T08:14:04-07:00","id":1376114,"title":"","content":"Are the bookmarks in anyone else's e-copy a little odd? I just opened up mine, and there were a bunch of tags labeled &quot;_GOBACK&quot;. It was actually a little creepy, for a second. There's also one called &quot;I_swear_its_not_J_Petersen_&quot; which links to Pangloss. Anyway, I was wondering if this should be reported to errata, or if it's an issue on my end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T08:30:18-07:00","id":1376116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1375557#post1375557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, are the Tremere supposed to be the Lower Depth counterparts to Scelesti now? Is the 'Seventh Dragon' that spoke to them at Chur implied to be some sort of demon they feed souls to?</div> </div> </div> </div>This used to have an answer more or less in LHP - it was a bound that dove into the Oroboros at the edge of the Abyss and grew into a paradoxical watchtower, but I think due to 2nd Edition's renewed focus on Mysteries, they made the Tremere central truth a Mystery. Also, there's been some suggestion that the Tremere do know more about souls and they may be right about certain things, so having their central truth canonically sprout from Lies probably needed to be adjusted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T11:28:14-07:00","id":1376126,"title":"","content":"I would still like a true Infernalist Legacy, but I suppose that would require a full Inferno update for 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T12:03:12-07:00","id":1376131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1376126#post1376126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would still like a true Infernalist Legacy, but I suppose that would require a full Inferno update for 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would such a Legacy be considered still be a very playable one? I would he sad if not","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date: