13:12-07:00","id":1376143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1376139#post1376139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As playable as Scelesti, Banishers, and Tremere. So mechanically supported but a potentially awkward mix with other PCs usually, but could be awesome in certain campaigns.<br /> <br /> For less inherently antagonistic \u201cdemonic\u201d Mages, you have Goetic Legacies like the Clauvicularus and the Bene Ashmedai, as well as Mastigos Summoners of Pandemonium Demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh ok. Well in that case, I'm fine with that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T14:37:12-07:00","id":1383038,"title":"","content":"Updated PDF is now up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T12:15:51-07:00","id":1383191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1383038#post1383038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Updated PDF is now up!</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone know what the changes are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T18:36:11-07:00","id":1383263,"title":"","content":"So, I was re-reading this earlier today, and popped up a question, and then some fun idle story seed shit.<br /> <br /> Question: Strictly speaking, nothing prevents a Prelate from becoming a Nasnas, yeah? The Prelate Merit isn't credited back upon the Joining, yeah?<br /> <br /> Story thought one: Man, idigam versus mage is fun, but Idigam against appropriately empowered Thyrsus Nasnas? That's a conflict it'd be hella fun to see Uratha and Awakened unravel.<br /> <br /> Story thought 2: So, Bellerophon Group mage dedicated to figuring out the big secrets behind the Greater Tulpa commits to acts that attack a Mage's Wisdom (for funsies, assume antinomian rotes) and drops so far down that they become a Rapt with a fault that basically keeps this up-ie, the Faultleads to them generating more Rapt for study.<br /> <br /> My mind took this setup and went extra just cause and made the particular character a (Legion) Guardian keeping an eye on an Adamantine Arrow cabal that was flirting with the edge and dug into the persona too deeply prior to becoming Rapt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T19:16:06-07:00","id":1383269,"title":"","content":"Favorite part so far is the Scelesti chapter, but as a long time Seers of the Throne fan I'm really happy to see some more Lesser Ministry info and Prelacy write ups too, especially since they were massive teases in Signs of Sorcery with that wonderfully undetailed list...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T12:42:32-07:00","id":1392278,"title":"","content":"The art direction for this book is way off. I mean, if it's a book about Horrors, then the arts should have more horrific images. Especially the front cover. It looks like some girl is jerking off a guy in a rave party. Those images would have been fine if it was more for social situations in MtA in another book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25803-omichli","name":"Omichli","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T01:09:44-07:00","id":1392442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omichli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1374172-nameless-and-accursed-on-dtrpg?p=1392278#post1392278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The art direction for this book is way off. I mean, if it's a book about Horrors, then the arts should have more horrific images. Especially the front cover. It looks like some girl is jerking off a guy in a rave party. Those images would have been fine if it was more for social situations in MtA in another book.</div> </div> </div> </div>That cover is literally seconds before Lucy Sulphate uses magic to control the crowd and trample a guy to death, which leads to her attempting suicide. So, the horror is in knowing the context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T02:10:18-07:00","id":1392452,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately that requires knowing the context in the first place, which requires both having read (or heard about) a specific short story as well as recognising that's what the cover refers to. A cover is generally supposed to draw the interest of potential buyers which this largely fails to do due to how few, even among fans of the game, who recognises the context to be able to find it interesting.<br /> I also want to mention that the context is the wrong kind of horror. Lucy Sulphate is a standin for PCs, making this a highly personal horror, showcasing how monstrous and twisted even regular mages can be, while the book is mostly about antagonists who are monstrous even when it comes to mages. The two big draws are the Tremere and the Scelesti (the latter being specifically referred to in the title) with Banishers being third, so it would be fitting to have a situation relating to one of those groups as the cover.<br /> I personally would've gone with something Tremere related (since Scelesti might confuse people to think the book is mostly about the Abyss), like having a mage in the process of stealing a soul or a mage standing over/moving away from an apathetic soulless victim. Well, a little more dynamic than that, but I'm not an artist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T08:03:07-07:00","id":1392532,"title":"","content":"Accurate. Iirc the guy she kills has been stalking her and she was getting premonitions that he was going to kill her so from the clues he seems like he was the kind of guy that would show up in this book. The cover doesn\u2019t tell that story that well though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T19:26:49-07:00","id":1509426,"title":"","content":"Count me in the camp that finds the temptation to go Scelesti pretty weak. An Act of Hubris for 1 Reach? I can't see anyone taking that deal. If you go full Nasnasi it's not as bad, but still not quite tempting enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}